# hep-genesis config for the Mu2e gpvms. setup.sh copies this to
# $HG_DATA_DIR/.env (default /exp/mu2e/data/users/$USER/hep-genesis-data/.env)
# and points HEP_ENV_FILE at it.
#
# Every hep_genesis module loads this file with override=True: values here win
# over your shell (except DISPATCH_REMOTE / DISPATCH_TARGET). Empty values
# count as unset. The hep-genesis-*-auth commands write their tokens back into
# this file. Full list of settings: backend/.env.example.
#
# Data locations (HEP_PROJECTS_DIR, HEP_STAGING_DIR, ...) are exported by
# setup.sh, not set here.

# ── LLM ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: gpt-oss-120b on the Fermilab vLLM service (same as kb-mcp). No key
# needed; "notused" fills the slot. Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works.
LLM_URL=https://vllm.fnal.gov/v1
LLM_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b
LLM_API_KEY=notused

# ALCF inference gateway instead: run `hep-genesis-alcf-inference-auth` once,
# then set LLM_URL/LLM_MODEL to the ALCF endpoint and model.
# LLM_URL=https://inference-api.alcf.anl.gov/resource_server/sophia/vllm/v1

# Optional per-stage overrides, each falling back to the LLM_* above:
# LLM_{SURVEY,PLAN,WORKER,CRITIC,REPORT,QUICK}_{URL,MODEL,API_KEY}
# (PLANNER/SYNTHESIS are legacy aliases of PLAN/REPORT; see agent/llm_factory.py).
#
# Other endpoints (e.g. Fermilab LiteLLM for Claude) are easier to add in the
# web UI's Models panel: it writes <data>/models.json, never this file, and
# the endpoint made active there wins over the LLM_* above (docs/WEB.md).

# ── Research budget (CLI and web UI runs) ───────────────────────────────
# Defaults: 4 waves, 5 parallel workers, 200 tool calls, 120 minutes.
# HEP_RESEARCH_MAX_WAVES=2
# HEP_RESEARCH_WORKERS=3
# HEP_RESEARCH_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=60
# HEP_RESEARCH_WALL_CLOCK_MIN=30

# ── Tool-call timeout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Seconds a single tool call may take before the model is told it timed out
# and the run carries on (default 300; 0 = no limit). Per-server values go
# in servers.json: "timeouts": {"kb": 600}. CLI: --tool-timeout.
# HEP_TOOL_TIMEOUT_S=300

# ── HPC dispatch (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment and fill from backend/.env.example when using Polaris/Perlmutter.
# DISPATCH_TARGET=polaris
# ALCF_USERNAME=
# ALCF_PROJECT=
# ALCF_WORKDIR=/lus/eagle/projects/<project>/<user>/<workdir>
# NERSC_USERNAME=
# NERSC_PROJECT=
# NERSC_WORKDIR=/pscratch/sd/<x>/<user>/hep_genesis
# GCP_ENDPOINT_ID=
